Seeded captures for the Wireshark/tshark lab (tools-wireshark-001).

capture.pcap — mixed traffic inside the fictional 10.10.10.0/24 lab network:
  * workstation 10.10.10.5  (analyst's view of a "victim" host)
  * web server  10.10.10.20  (intranet.lan — cleartext HTTP login!)
  * dns/gateway 10.10.10.1
  * 10.10.10.30:443          (TLS ClientHello — where does it go?)
  Look for: ARP, DNS, TCP, HTTP, TLS, ICMP — then follow the HTTP login
  TCP stream (tshark -z follow,tcp,ascii,0), spot the cleartext credentials,
  and find the DNS-TXT exfiltration to exfil.evil-dns.net.

dns-exfil.pcap — a focused DNS-tunneling capture: TXT queries carrying
base64-looking data chunks to data.exfil.evil-dns.net, with a little
ordinary DNS noise mixed in.

Useful tshark invocations:
  tshark -r capture.pcap -q -z io,phs            # protocol hierarchy
  tshark -r capture.pcap -Y dns -T fields -e dns.qry.name -e dns.qry.type
  tshark -r capture.pcap -q -z follow,tcp,ascii,0 # follow the login stream
  tshark -r capture.pcap -Y http -T fields -e http.authorization
